[ti:Day 04]

[00:00.00]victim [ˈvɪktɪm]n. 受害者；牺牲者；牺牲品 例 Many businesses have offered large amounts of financial aid or material relief to the victims of the earthquake. 搭 fall victim to sb./sth. 因某人或某事而受到伤 害
[00:18.72]precocious [prɪˈkəʊʃəs]a. 早熟的；(知识、能力等)较早发展 的；超前的 例 Adolescents are among the most voracious and precocious users of mobile Internet services.
[00:33.60]culminate [ˈkʌlmɪneɪt]vi. 达到极点；告终 vt. 使达到极点 例 He is the driving force on bilateral talks on trade, which should culminate in the next few months in a meeting of foreign ministers. 搭 culminate in 以…告终
[00:53.52]right-sizing [ˈraɪtsaɪzɪŋ]n. 合理精简，裁员
[00:57.60]earnest [ˈɜːnɪst]a. 认真的，诚挚的 n. 定金；保证金；预 示；保证 例 Earnest money is usually paid to bind a contract between the importer and exporter. 搭 in earnest 认真的(地)
[01:12.72]capability [ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti]n. 才能，能力；技能；尚未发挥的 天资和素质 搭 capability to do sth./of doing sth. 做某事的 能力
[01:22.68]affidavit [ˌæfəˈdeɪvɪt]n. 宣誓书；书面陈述 例 My father was asked to sign an affidavit of financial support.
[01:32.88]mechanisation [ˌmekənaɪˈzeɪʃn]n. 机械化
[01:36.96]likelihood [ˈlaɪklihʊd]n. 可能，可能性 例 After you choose a proper partner, the likelihood of your success will increase.
[01:48.84]household [ˈhaʊshəʊld]a. 家庭的；日常的，家常的 n. 家 庭；一家人 搭 household allowance 安家费 / household appliance 家用电器 / household necessity 日用 必需品
[02:02.16]holistic [həʊˈlɪstɪk]a. 整体的；全盘的，全面的 例 The landowners at the Western ranch have been using holistic management to streamline costs and enhance profits. 搭 holistic approach 整体分析
[02:20.28]finite [ˈfaɪnaɪt]a. 有限的；有限制的；限定的 例 In a world of finite resources, we need to change how we work to make the best use of every resource we have.
[02:34.44]boundary [ˈbaʊndri]n. 分界线；边界；范围，范畴 例 Air pollution respects no boundaries and we must make common efforts to protect the environment.
[02:48.24]yardstick [ˈjɑːdstɪk]n. 码尺；准绳；衡量标准；评价标准 例 With patents becoming a new yardstick for performance evaluation, an increasing number of Chinese scholars have filed a patent application.
[03:07.20]sweepstake [ˈswiːpsteɪk]n. 赌金独得；彩票
[03:11.04]correspondent [ˌkɒrəˈspɒndənt]n. 通讯员；记者；异地代理商 (或客户)；(异地)代理银行 a. 一致的，符合的 例 The following details of the organisation and routine have come into the possession of your correspondent.
[03:30.00]snobbish [ˈsnɒbɪʃ]a. 势利的；假充内行的 例 He is snobbish about mobile phones.
[03:37.08]eminent [ˈemɪnənt]a. 突出的，明显的；显赫的，杰出的 例 The eminent speaker will use case studies to show how design can make businesses more efficient and desirable.
[03:52.44]relinquish [rɪˈlɪŋkwɪʃ]vt. 放弃；让与(财产、权利等)；把… 交给；让渡 例 He was forced to relinquish his job. 搭 relinquish...to 把…交给…
[04:04.20]frenzy [ˈfrenzi]n. 极度的激动；疯狂；狂热 vt. 使狂乱； 使发狂 例 The country now is gripped by a frenzy of nationalism.
[04:14.28]tertiary [ˈtɜːʃəri]a. 第三的；第三位的
[04:17.64]designate [ˈdezɪɡneɪt]vt. 指派，委任；指定 例 With the increasing demand for wilderness recreation, they plan to designate 60 percent of the area suitable to develop wilderness entertainment.
[04:36.60]keynote [ˈkiːnəʊt]n. 主旨，要旨；基调 vt. 给…定基调； (讨论会等上)做主题发言 例 The keynote of the meeting is innovation. 搭 keynote address 政治性集会中的政策演讲 / keynote speaker 主题发言人 / keynote speech (讨论会等的)主题发言 / set the keynote 定下基 调
[04:57.36]block [blɒk]n. 区组；大宗，大量 vt. 阻塞；阻碍，妨 碍；限制使用(货币、财产等) 例 She had a block transaction on the Hong Kong stock Exchange. 搭 a block of 大量，大宗 / block off 封锁，封 闭
[05:12.24]quay [kiː]n. (装卸)码头
[05:14.28]revive [rɪˈvaɪv]v. (使)恢复；(使)振兴；(使)再流行；(使) 生效 例 As soon as the price picks up, enquiries will immediately revive.
[05:25.92]unveil [ˌʌnˈveɪl]vt. 使除去面纱；揭露；展示；揭幕；使 公之于众 vi. 除去面纱；显露 例 Ford unveiled the latest trends the brand would bring to its Chinese clientele last Monday.
[05:41.16]plummet [ˈplʌmɪt]vi. 垂直落下；(价格、水平等)骤然跌落 n. 铅锤；坠子；重荷 搭 plummet lamp 垂灯
[05:48.36]marketing [ˈmɑːkɪtɪŋ]n. 促销；营销；销售活动
[05:52.20]expropriation [eksˌprəʊpriˈeɪʃn]n. 没收(财产)；征用(土地) 例 Land expropriation is quite common now when building shopping malls.
[06:04.92]acceptability [əkˌseptəˈbɪləti]n. 可承兑性；可接受性 例 It is usually the customer that ultimately determines the acceptability of the product.
[06:18.96]segment [ˈseɡmənt]n. 部分；部门 [seɡˈment]v. 分割(市场)
[06:24.00]abject [ˈæbdʒekt]a. 可怜的，凄惨的，绝望无助的 例 The attempt to take over the company has finally turned out to be an abject failure.
[06:36.12]solicit [səˈlɪsɪt]v. 请求；招揽(生意)；招募(人员)；征 求；征集 搭 solicit for 征求；招徕
[06:42.96]ongoing [ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ]a. 前进的；进行中的
[06:46.20]embed [ɪmˈbed]vt. 把…嵌入(或埋入、插入)，扎牢；使 深留于脑中 例 It's impossible to embed other programming language here. 搭 be embedded in 根植于
[06:58.80]exhibitor [ɪɡˈzɪbɪtə(r)]n. 参展者，参展商 例 Exhibitors from all industries are invited to the hi-tech exhibition once a year.
[07:11.04]format [ˈfɔːmæt]n. 设计，安排；格式，样式；版式 vt. 使格式化 例 We will discuss the advantages of one format over the other.
[07:21.72]abuse [əˈbjuːz]v. 滥用，妄用(权力等) [əˈbjuːs]n. 滥用，妄用 例 The position of General Manager is potentially open to abuse. 搭 abuse of sth. 滥用…派 abusive a. 被滥用 的；腐败的(例：abusive practices 腐败行为)
[07:39.96]seminar [ˈsemɪnɑː(r)]n. 研讨班，研讨小组
[07:43.56]charter [ˈtʃɑːtə(r)]n. 特许状，许可证；(船只、飞机等的) 包租；包租契约；证书 vt. 特许成立(公司等)；发 执照给 例 Charter schools, an alternative to other public schools, are part of the public education system and are not allowed to charge tuition.
[08:05.16]gearing [ˈɡɪərɪŋ]n. 配称(英国术语，指股份资本和定息资 本之间的关系)；举债经营；联动比率；齿轮作用 例 What makes the industry ripe for restructuring is its operational gearing.
[08:19.80]relatively [ˈrelətɪvli]ad. 相对地；相关地；相当地 例 We have to make do with relatively small profit margins at the beginning.
[08:31.56]manifest [ˈmænɪfest]a. 明显的，明了的 vt. 表明；证明； 使显露 n. 舱单；载货目录，载货清单
[08:38.04]lecturer [ˈlektʃərə(r)]n. (大学或学院中的)授课者；讲师； 演讲者
[08:43.20]claim [kleɪm]v. 索取；对…提出要求；宣称，声称 n. 索赔；要求；声称 例 We have to put in a claim against you for all the losses sustained. 搭 claim back 要求退回 / lay claim to 坚持对… 的所有权 / put in a claim for sth. 为某物损坏提 出索赔
[09:01.80]amount [əˈmaʊnt]v. 总计；相当于 n. 总数，总额；量， 数量；总的价值(或意义) 例 Taken together, the economies of the European Union countries amount to just under 24% of the global economy. 搭 any amount (of) 大量(的) / be of little amount 无多大价值
[09:23.28]occupation [ˌɒkjuˈpeɪʃn]n. 职业；(土地、建筑等的)使用；居 住；占有，占用
[09:29.04]outpost [ˈaʊtpəʊst]n. 前哨；哨站；(组织的)边远分部 搭 outpost officer 驻外官员
[09:35.52]spoilage [ˈspɔɪlɪdʒ]n. 损坏；损坏物；食物变质
[09:39.36]glitch [ɡlɪtʃ]n. 小过失；小故障；运转失灵 例 I cannot work out the marketing schedule today because the computer program has a glitch. 搭 technical glitch 技术故障
[09:54.12]depreciate [dɪˈpriːʃieɪt]vt. 使贬值；跌价 例 The financial crisis caused many overseas assets to depreciate against the yuan.
[10:06.48]trajectory [trəˈdʒektəri]n. 轨道；轨迹 例 I can hardly believe the upward trajectory of commodity prices in recent years.
[10:18.36]impeccable [ɪmˈpekəbl]a. 无错误的；无瑕疵的；极好的 例 As the representative of the company, her manners at the party were impeccable.
[10:30.84]exceptional [ɪkˈsepʃənl]a. 优越的，杰出的；额外的；特殊 的，异常的 例 Exceptional cases should be handled differently.
[10:41.40]cornerstone [ˈkɔːnəstəʊn]n. 基石；基础 例 Trade has been a cornerstone of our growth and global development.
[10:51.96]expand [ɪkˈspænd]v. (使)扩大，(使)扩展；详述 例 Expanding the business is always on his mind.
[11:00.48]manuscript [ˈmænjuskrɪpt]n. 手稿，原稿；(手)抄本 a. 手写 的 搭 manuscript copy 手写稿；原稿 / novel in manuscript 小说手稿
[11:10.68]cheque [tʃek]n. 支票 例 You may cash in this cheque at all times and all places. 搭 make out a cheque 开支票
[11:20.28]prowl [praʊl]v./n. 潜行(以寻觅)；徘徊(于) 例 The company remains on the prowl to make some recent big purchases.
[11:30.72]proclaim [prəˈkleɪm]vt. 声明；宣布；公开赞扬 搭 proclaim a law 公布一项法令
[11:36.84]confidential [ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl]a. 极受信任的；参与机密的；秘密 的，机密的 例 The employer has always worried about his employees' taking confidential information with them out the door.
[11:53.76]fragile [ˈfrædʒaɪl]a. 脆的；易碎的；脆弱的 例 Though the global business conditions have been much improved, the local investors' confidence remains fragile.
[12:09.12]back [bæk]a. 到期未付的，拖欠的；倒的，反向的 vt. 支持；使后退 n. 背部；力气 例 Due to the demand for these goods exceeding the supply, we were on a huge back order. 搭 back out 不履行；食言 / back up 支持 / break the back of 完成(任务的)绝大部分
[12:28.56]managerial [ˌmænəˈdʒɪəriəl]a. 管理人的；管理上的；经营上 的
[12:33.60]capacity [kəˈpæsəti]n. 生产能力；能量；容量；能力；身 份，资格 例 What really concerns me is that there should be so little willingness or capacity to do anything. 搭 in the capacity of 以…的资格 baby bust 生育低谷期 例 The figure reflects a transition from baby boom to baby bust. 这个图表反映了从婴儿潮到 生育低谷的过渡。
[13:00.96]publicity [pʌbˈlɪsəti]n. 公开(性)；(媒体的)宣传；宣传品， 广告
[13:06.12]slogan [ˈsləʊɡən]n. 标语
[13:08.52]obsolete [ˈɒbsəliːt]vt. 废弃，淘汰；使变得过时 a. 废弃 的，淘汰的；陈旧的，过时的
[13:14.52]utilise [ˈjuːtəlaɪz]vt. 利用，使用 例 He expected to utilise China's capital and market advantage to drive the company's development.
[13:27.72]pare [peə(r)]vt. 剥；削；削减
[13:30.24]outgoing [ˈaʊtɡəʊɪŋ]a. 外出的，出发的；外发的；(外卖食 品等)准备外运的，外卖的；即将离职的；外向的 n. [pl.] 开支，开销
[13:38.76]origin [ˈɒrɪdʒɪn]n. 起源；产地；背景，[常pl.] 出身
[13:42.96]credible [ˈkredəbl]a. 可信的，可靠的 例 The failure of the US to develop any credible path for fiscal tightening is also grossly irresponsible.
[13:56.76]quell [kwel]vt. 镇压；消除，减轻 例 These latest measures have done nothing to quell the public's suspicion about the increase of house prices.
[14:10.44]misfortune [ˌmɪsˈfɔːtʃuːn]n. 不幸；厄运；逆境；灾难，灾祸 例 He has suffered a good deal of misfortune over the years.
[14:21.12]retool [ˌriːˈtuːl]vt. 更换工具，更新设备；重组，改革 vi. 更换工具，更新设备 例 They were forced to retool their business strategy in light of global realities.
[14:35.04]cabinet [ˈkæbɪnət]n. 橱柜；内阁；密室
[14:38.28]portion [ˈpɔːʃn]n. 部分；一份 vt. 分配 例 He takes a portion of his salary each month for savings.
[14:47.16]consensual [kənˈsenʃuəl]a. 经双方同意而产生的，两愿的； 例 Probably the most important attribute of a contract is the consensual relationship between two parties. 搭 consensual marriage 双方同意的婚姻
[15:05.76]world-class [ˌwɜːldˈklɑːs]a. 世界级的
[15:09.48]remonstrate [ˈremənstreɪt]v. 抗议；告诫 搭 remonstrate against 抗议；反对
